    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "It's not even a block though. A block implies i'll eventually get unstuck. This is different. I can feel my talent just... evaporating. If i keep going, i'm just going to become a parody of myself. I'd rather stop now while I'm still 'something' than live to see myself become a joke of a person who used to be good at something.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That feeling of fading away is incredibly painful, but please don't mistake a phase of creative struggle for a permanent loss of talent. Instead of viewing it as evaporation, consider this a period of necessary evolution where your skills are shifting. Instead of trying to replicate your past success, experiment with entirely new styles or mediums to see what resonates now. Your worth isn't tied to the quality of your last piece of writing.",
